Summary: winemac: HostWindows option; a native host application shows the windows
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: dlls/winemac.drv (new cocoa_host.m; hooks in cocoa_window.m,
 cocoa_app.m, macdrv_main.c, surface.c, window.c, opengl.c); the OpenGL
 part grew out of the IOSurface probe of 2026-11-17. Written for
 wine-mac-builds.
Source: none published
Upstream: no
Why: An app that embeds Wine wants a program's windows inside its own
 windows, scaled or letterboxed as it likes, and the input back, without
 the program putting windows of its own on screen. The protocol is
 docs/app-embedded-protocol.md, its wire format
 docs/app-embedded-protocol.h (copied here as wmh_protocol.h). With
 HostWindows ("y"; HKCU\Software\Wine\Mac Driver, or per program under
 AppDefaults\<exe>\Mac Driver) and WINEMAC_HOST_SERVICE naming a host's
 Mach service, the driver does the handshake before Cocoa starts. If it
 succeeds, each window's Cocoa functions send messages to the host instead
 of making an NSWindow, window surfaces are drawn into IOSurfaces the host
 is sent (up to three per window, each handed back by surface_release),
 and a receive thread turns the host's input, focus, close and quit
 events into the usual macdrv events. Without the variable, or if the host
 doesn't answer in 10 seconds, the plain driver is used and an err: line
 says why. NSApplication still runs (for the main-thread dispatch, event
 queues, displays, the pasteboard and keyboard layouts), but the process
 shows no window, Dock icon or menu bar of its own. The design doc said
 no NSApplication; keeping it changed much less of the driver.
 OpenGL (and Direct3D through wined3d, and DirectDraw wrappers that use
 OpenGL) goes to the host as views: each client surface is a view of its
 window, and framebuffer 0 of its drawable is remapped, in the GL functions
 the driver hands out, to an FBO on an IOSurface from the view's pool;
 each present finishes, sends the surface (bottom-up) and points the FBO
 at a free one. Win32u, opengl32 and wined3d are unchanged. The context
 is kept current with no view attached. The cursor goes to the host too:
 a system cursor by its NSCursor name, an image as an IOSurface (the
 first frame of an animated one), hidden; SetCursorPos and ClipCursor are
 passed on, and the cursor position is the last one the host reported.
 The host can ask for a window's size limits (WM_GETMINMAXINFO) and say
 a resize is starting; the driver posts those as queries without waiting
 and answers with window_min_max. Repeated identical messages aren't
 resent.
 Covered: the handshake, windows, GDI surfaces, OpenGL views, cursor,
 size limits, keys, mouse, focus, close and quit. Not yet: animated
 cursors, window shape and alpha, Metal and Vulkan, displays_get, the
 resize-size query, and
 window_get_frame as a call (the driver keeps the frame it last set or the
 host last reported).
Programs: Second Chance (an app that embeds Wine): shows a program inside
 its own window
Uncertain: each present waits for glFinish. Windows of other processes as
 owners aren't supported (v1).
Applies to: wine 11.22 (macfixes, after 0068)
Status: 2026-11-22 (focus activation): window_focus carries
 WMH_FOCUS_ACTIVATE when the plain driver would activate the app (within
 2 s of a global hotkey or a tray icon click), so a host needn't activate
 on every focus. Test host, Notepad (1 run): focus came without the flag,
 as expected; the flagged case not exercised.
 2026-11-22 (padding under emulated modes): a fullscreen window
 under EmulateModeset has a surface padded beyond its window rect (to a
 multiple of 128 px); the plain driver hides the padding with its black
 mask (macdrv_set_window_mask), which host mode skips. The surface flush
 now paints the padding black in host mode. Test host on meeka, 1 run
 each: fullscreen-gdi-centred (2160x1440 window, 2176x1536 surface) had
 grey padding on host8 and black with this; White Wolf's padding (columns
 1920-2175, x 2240-2496 on screen: the white strip Second Chance saw) is
 black with it.
 2026-11-22 (integration, host8): Second Chance's integration tests of
 every bundle (disc, download, Her download, Big Fish trial and owned,
 Steam) passed with games' windows hosted; the fixes needed were all in
 its host. Japanese conversion is open, and not a host-mode bug: with
 Kotoeri's prediction popup or candidate list showing, Space doesn't
 convert (the kana stay marked) and Return commits nothing (no callback
 from the input method). Plain mode does the same (traced in a Screen
 Slots slot, 2 runs; passing key-ups to the input context too didn't
 change it).
 2026-11-21 (integration): Second Chance's integration test of
 SkiFree passed on host6 with the game's window shown by its app bundle's
 host (captured, clicked and quit through it; 1 run). HostWindows set per
 game exe (AppDefaults), so explorer, Steam and the Game Manager stay on
 the plain driver.
 2026-11-21 (input methods): the driver calls the host (ime_key) for
 each key Wine gives an open IME, and replays the marked and committed
 text the host's input context produced through macdrv_ime_set_text;
 ime_rect and ime_clear stand in for the composition rect and
 clear_ime_text. The host's KEYBOARD_CHANGED now makes the driver reread
 the input source (it was dropped). Shown with tools/wmh-testhost
 (WMH_TESTHOST_IME, scripted answers) and Notepad in a Screen Slots slot
 with Japanese Romaji selected (macOS 26.7), 1 run: "a" gave the marked
 text and Return committed it, ImeToAsciiEx traced both, Notepad's caret
 moved one wide character with no new line. Without an input method the
 keys reached Notepad directly, with no ime_key calls (1 run). Not yet
 with a real input method in a host.
 2026-11-21 (drag and drop): files dragged onto a window: the host's
 drag messages become the plain driver's drag-drop queries, answered with
 drag_done; the driver opens the drag pasteboard by name. Shown with
 tools/wmh-testhost (WMH_TESTHOST_DROP, a file URL on a named pasteboard)
 and Notepad on meeka, 1 run: enter, update (ops copy) and drop were
 accepted and Notepad opened the file. Not yet through Second Chance's
 host or a real Finder drag.
 2026-11-21 (minimize, maximize, real host): Second Chance's host on host6,
 Notepad: Zoom, Cmd-M and the Dock, and fullscreen in a Space work. After
 a Dock restore Notepad came back about 4 pt narrower and 24 pt shorter
 than its window: Wine works out the restored rect from the frame using
 the minimized window's rects (no non-client area). The plain driver
 corrects it with the frame change that follows every deminiaturize; the
 host didn't send one. With the test host sending it, the rects came back
 right (1 run). The protocol now says to send it.
 2026-11-21 (minimize, maximize): the host's WINDOW_MINIMIZE_REQUESTED and
 WINDOW_MAXIMIZE_REQUESTED, run on the main thread as the plain driver
 does (the receive thread can't call win32u: the first try hung it in
 NtUserGetWindowLongW). Shown with tools/wmh-testhost and Notepad on
